# Release tarballs are NOT committed. SHA256SUMS + SHA256SUMS.asc are, and
# they are signed by the builder threshold — that is the trust anchor, and it
# makes any later download of the tarball verifiable. Committing ~86MB of
# already-compressed bytes per release per arch adds no integrity, only
# permanent history. See 'Why the tarball is not committed' in CLAUDE.md.
upstream/*.tar.gz

provenance.json
contents-manifest.json
sbom.spdx.json
keys/trusted-fingerprints.txt.candidate
